title: should rewrite relationships, including text links, that pointed to the node with the link
pid: 3735bdab-1a18-4858-aa29-6f7dc21ee046
body: |2-
  That is, suppose node C (container)
  contains node L (link)
  which is just a link to node T (target),
  and node S (source) links to L.
  Replacing L with a contains relationship from C to T
  orphans the link that went from S to L.

  This is probably true of other relationships to L, too.
